{
  "diagnosis": {
    "summary": "The creature falls after a lateral push because the standing controller's balance feedback is too weak to arrest the momentum-driven COM divergence. The extrapolated COM margin (xcom) goes negative immediately at push onset and never recovers, indicating the ankle torque demand never reaches the actuator limit but is simply insufficient to generate the required angular acceleration. Two of three seeds fall with similar timing (~1.4 s after push end), while the surviving seed starts with a more favorable initial pitch and COM velocity.",
    "hypotheses": [
      {
        "id": "H1",
        "mechanism": "Insufficient balance_gain: the ankle torque demanded by the PD + balance controller (peak 1.21 Nm) is far below the 60 Nm limit, yet the extrapolated COM margin (xcom) reaches -0.56 m and never recovers. The controller gain is too low to produce the angular acceleration needed to reverse the torso pitch rate (peak 0.47 rad/s) before the COM leaves the support polygon.",
        "evidence": [
          "forensics_seed0.actuation.ankle_peak_demand_Nm: 1.21",
          "forensics_seed0.actuation.torque_limit_Nm: 60.0",
          "forensics_seed0.actuation.ankle_demand_over_limit_peak: 0.02",
          "forensics_seed0.failure.xcom_margin_recovered_s: null",
          "forensics_seed0.support.min_xcom_margin_after_push_m: -0.562",
          "forensics_seed0.disturbance.peak_pitch_rate_within_1s_rad_s: 0.471"
        ],
        "competing": [
          "The torque limit itself could be too low, but the demand is only 2% of the limit, so raising the limit would not change the applied torque unless the gain is also increased.",
          "Foot friction is low, but peak slip speed is only 0.166 m/s and slipping fraction is 1.3%, so slip is not the primary cause."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "H2",
        "mechanism": "Foot length (0.05 m) yields a tiny support polygon (support length 0.008 m), so the COM margin before push is already negative (-0.042 m). The push impulse (3.75 Ns) easily drives the extrapolated COM far outside the support, and the small foot provides no lever arm to generate a large ground reaction moment.",
        "evidence": [
          "forensics_seed0.support.support_length_before_push_m: 0.0079",
          "forensics_seed0.support.com_margin_before_push_m: -0.0422",
          "forensics_seed0.support.xcom_margin_before_push_m: -0.0804",
          "forensics_seed0.disturbance.impulse_Ns: 3.75",
          "creature.body.foot_length: 0.05",
          "creature.derived.foot_to_leg_ratio: 0.0833"
        ],
        "competing": [
          "Increasing foot length also moves the ankle joint forward, changing the leg geometry and potentially the standing posture; however, the primary effect is a larger support base.",
          "A wider stance (not editable) would also increase support, but only foot_length is available."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "H3",
        "mechanism": "Low joint PD stiffness (kp=150) and damping (kd=8) allow the stance to deform under the push, increasing the effective COM height and reducing the ankle's mechanical advantage. The peak pitch rate (0.47 rad/s) and large pitch excursion (1.6 rad at fall) suggest the legs buckle rather than push back.",
        "evidence": [
          "controller.stand.kp: 150.0",
          "controller.stand.kd: 8.0",
          "forensics_seed0.disturbance.peak_abs_pitch_within_1s_rad: 0.158",
          "forensics_seed0.disturbance.peak_pitch_rate_within_1s_rad_s: 0.471",
          "seeds[0].max_abs_pitch_rad: 1.6",
          "forensics_seed0.failure.pitch_at_fall_rad: -1.0"
        ],
        "competing": [
          "The peak pitch within 1 s of push is only 0.158 rad, so the large pitch at fall develops later, likely from the unrecovered xcom margin rather than immediate stance collapse.",
          "Increasing kp/kd could make the controller oscillatory or amplify sensor noise; the current values may be near a stability boundary."
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "proposals": [
    {
      "id": "P1",
      "hypothesis": "H1",
      "category": "control",
      "edits": [
        {
          "param": "stand.balance_gain",
          "op": "scale",
          "value": 1.25,
          "target": "both"
        }
      ],
      "retune_controller": false,
      "prediction": {
        "metric": "fall_rate",
        "direction": "decrease",
        "expected_change": "From 67% to 0-33% (0-1 falls in 3 seeds); xcom_margin_recovered_s becomes finite in fallen seeds."
      },
      "tradeoffs": "Higher balance_gain increases ankle torque demand for a given pitch error, risking actuator saturation (currently at 2% of limit) and possible high-frequency oscillations if the PD loop is not damped enough. May cause jerky ankle motion on uneven terrain.",
      "confidence": 0.75,
      "verification": "Check forensics_seed0.actuation.ankle_demand_over_limit_peak stays < 0.5 and fraction_samples_saturated_push_to_fall remains 0.0; verify xcom_margin_recovered_s < fall_time_s in previously fallen seeds."
    },
    {
      "id": "P2",
      "hypothesis": "H2",
      "category": "morphology",
      "edits": [
        {
          "param": "foot_length",
          "op": "scale",
          "value": 1.5,
          "target": "both"
        }
      ],
      "retune_controller": false,
      "prediction": {
        "metric": "fall_rate",
        "direction": "decrease",
        "expected_change": "From 67% to 0-33%; support_length_before_push_m increases from 0.008 m to ~0.012 m, making pre-push com_margin positive and reducing min_xcom_margin_after_push_m magnitude."
      },
      "tradeoffs": "Longer foot increases leg mass (leg_density fixed), raising inertia and shifting COM forward; may require slight retuning of stand_hip/stand_knee to maintain nominal posture. Larger foot could increase sticking/slipping transitions on rough ground.",
      "confidence": 0.65,
      "verification": "Verify forensics_seed0.support.support_length_before_push_m > 0.01 m and com_margin_before_push_m > 0; check that min_height_ratio stays > 0.9 in surviving seeds (no excessive crouch)."
    },
    {
      "id": "P3",
      "hypothesis": "H1+H3",
      "category": "combined",
      "edits": [
        {
          "param": "stand.balance_gain",
          "op": "scale",
          "value": 1.2,
          "target": "both"
        },
        {
          "param": "stand.kd",
          "op": "scale",
          "value": 1.25,
          "target": "both"
        }
      ],
      "retune_controller": false,
      "prediction": {
        "metric": "fall_rate",
        "direction": "decrease",
        "expected_change": "From 67% to 0%; increased balance_gain provides more corrective torque, while higher kd damps the resulting pitch oscillation, preventing overshoot and reducing peak_pitch_rate_within_1s_rad_s."
      },
      "tradeoffs": "Combined change may over-damp the stance, slowing recovery from smaller disturbances. Higher kd increases torque demand during rapid pitch changes, but ankle_demand_over_limit_peak should remain well below 1.0.",
      "confidence": 0.7,
      "verification": "Confirm ankle_demand_over_limit_peak < 0.3 and peak_pitch_rate_within_1s_rad_s drops below 0.3 rad/s; ensure xcom_margin_recovered_s occurs within 1.0 s after push end in all seeds."
    }
  ]
}

